From de6d043385f073dcb0a876a237e78210579b65b2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 08:09:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] dvbridge: the player information says when a view setting
 keeps the ordinary output

A picture that is zoomed, stretched or shifted out of the raster is not
drawn by the native Dolby Vision output: the renderer keeps it on the
ordinary one, by design. The Dolby Vision page of the player
information then gave the reason as "not available for this video",
which is what it says when it knows none, although nothing of the
display or the output stood in the way and the setting was the user's
own.

The renderer now tells the window system when a picture asks for
native output, the output takes it, the picture cannot be placed, and
the view is not the default one (zoom, pixel ratio, vertical shift or
non-linear stretch); the page gives "the view settings (zoom, stretch
or shift)" as the reason (hades.dv.reason = view). With the default
view, a picture that cannot be placed as it comes (a stream whose
pixels are not square) or that is rotated, which may be the stream's
own rotation, keeps the general reason. The reasons of the output keep
their precedence, and nothing about which pictures go where changes.

What it cannot tell: with a view that is not the default one but is
not what keeps the picture away either (a zoom out on a stream whose
pixels are not square), it still names the view.

Reviewed, and read again after its corrections; not seen on a display.
